      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Quantitative angiographic studies with use of cine-videodensitometry after maximal coronary vasodilation with nitroglycerin in 18 \"angiographically normal\" heart transplant recipients demonstrated significant loss of lumen diameter between years 1 and 3. When sensitive angiographic techniques are used, graft arteriopathy appears to be ubiquitous in heart transplant recipients."},
